# Build output for the reference implementation's ecosystem (ADR-005).
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Bytecode from the provisional Python gates under .github/scripts/ (ADR-006). These go
# away when the gates move into `aios check`; the entry stays until then.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# CI discovers tests with `unittest discover`, so this never appears there. It appears
# locally when someone reaches for pytest instead, and the documentation gate walks the
# filesystem rather than the index — so an ignored directory still trips it.
.pytest_cache/

# Scratch files. The development machine reads CI over the REST API with throwaway scripts,
# and `git add -A` has swept two of them into commits already.
.tmp-*
fmt.patch

# Local tool and editor state that is per-machine rather than per-project.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# OS noise.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Nothing under aios/ is ignored on purpose. It is project state, not build output, and
# an ignored state directory is a state directory that silently stops being reviewed.

# Written by the feedback-speed gate in CI; a measurement, not state.
speed.json

# The active mode. Session state, not project state: committing it would make one
# developer's mode everyone's.
.aios-mode

# Session state for autonomy: which tasks have begun without review, and which a human
# has approved. Both are per-session, not project state.
.aios-session
.aios-approval

# Observed test outcomes, for the three-strikes hard stop. Session state.
.aios-attempts
.aios-writer
.aios-probe.json

# ios board is generated. A stored view can be wrong forever; a rendered one only
# briefly. If it is ever written to a file, that file is not the source of truth.
board.md
